[0.3,"o","==========================================================================\r\n"]
[0.6,"o"," agentic-checkout-reference — an agent buys something, in three runs\r\n"]
[0.9,"o","==========================================================================\r\n"]
[1.2,"o","\r\n"]
[1.5,"o","An agent shops at a merchant and pays, inside limits a person\r\n"]
[1.8,"o","signed in advance. Run 1 stays inside them. Run 2 goes over the\r\n"]
[2.1,"o","threshold the person set for being asked, so a human confirms.\r\n"]
[2.4,"o","Run 3 makes five attempts to spend past the mandate, and all five\r\n"]
[2.7,"o","are refused.\r\n"]
[3,"o","Nothing here touches real money: the payment rail is a stub.\r\n"]
[3.3,"o","\r\n"]
[3.6,"o","HOW THIS DEMO IS WIRED\r\n"]
[3.9,"o","  merchant              in this process, over the MCP in-memory transport\r\n"]
[4.2,"o","  why                   so the demo can print the merchant’s own audit log\r\n"]
[4.5,"o","  stdio path            scripts/stdio-smoke.test.ts, against merchant/stdio.ts\r\n"]
[4.8,"o","  clock                 frozen at 2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z\r\n"]
[5.1,"o","  ids                   sequential, so two runs print the same text\r\n"]
[5.4,"o","  keys                  generated in memory; no private key is ever printed\r\n"]
[5.7,"o","\r\n"]
[8,"o","--------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n"]
[8.3,"o"," RUN 1 — the mandate covers the basket, so the agent just buys\r\n"]
[8.6,"o","--------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n"]
[8.9,"o","\r\n"]
[9.2,"o","THE MANDATE — what the principal signed\r\n"]
[9.5,"o","  principal-demo lets agent-buyer-1 spend at merchant-demo:\r\n"]
[9.8,"o","    up to £50.00 (5000 pence) in total\r\n"]
[10.1,"o","    at most £25.00 (2500 pence) in any one order\r\n"]
[10.4,"o","    in GBP and no other currency\r\n"]
[10.7,"o","    between 2026-10-25T00:00:00Z and 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z\r\n"]
[11,"o","    without asking up to £30.00 (3000 pence); above that a human must confirm\r\n"]
[11.3,"o","  Signed Ed25519 over the canonical claims. The merchant holds the\r\n"]
[11.6,"o","  issuer's public key, read from ACR_MANDATE_PUBLIC_KEY, and no other\r\n"]
[11.9,"o","  key material: the private key never leaves the issuer, and nothing\r\n"]
[12.2,"o","  derived from it is printed here.\r\n"]
[12.5,"o","\r\n"]
[12.8,"o","THE SAME MANDATE, AS IT TRAVELS\r\n"]
[13.1,"o","  {\r\n"]
[13.4,"o","    \"mandate_id\": \"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\",\r\n"]
[13.7,"o","    \"principal\": \"principal-demo\",\r\n"]
[14,"o","    \"agent\": \"agent-buyer-1\",\r\n"]
[14.3,"o","    \"merchant\": \"merchant-demo\",\r\n"]
[14.6,"o","    \"currency\": \"GBP\",\r\n"]
[14.9,"o","    \"amount_cap_minor\": 5000,\r\n"]
[15.2,"o","    \"per_transaction_cap_minor\": 2500,\r\n"]
[15.5,"o","    \"valid_from\": \"2026-10-25T00:00:00Z\",\r\n"]
[15.8,"o","    \"valid_until\": \"2026-10-26T00:00:00Z\",\r\n"]
[16.1,"o","    \"human_confirm_above_minor\": 3000,\r\n"]
[16.4,"o","    \"signature\": \"<Ed25519 over the ten fields above, base64url — not printed>\"\r\n"]
[16.7,"o","  }\r\n"]
[17,"o","\r\n"]
[17.3,"o","THE CONNECTION — what the agent and the merchant agreed to speak\r\n"]
[17.6,"o","  MCP revision          2025-11-25 (era legacy)\r\n"]
[17.9,"o","  That is the in-memory transport’s answer — an McpServer reached inside\r\n"]
[18.2,"o","  this process serves the 2025-era handshake — whereas a merchant spawned\r\n"]
[18.5,"o","  from merchant/stdio.ts negotiates 2026-07-28, which D75 records and\r\n"]
[18.8,"o","  scripts/stdio-smoke.test.ts asserts.\r\n"]
[19.1,"o","\r\n"]
[19.4,"o","WHAT THE AGENT DID — one line per step\r\n"]
[19.7,"o","   1  list_products  10 products in the catalogue\r\n"]
[20,"o","   2  create_cart    cart_000001, empty\r\n"]
[20.3,"o","   3  add_to_cart    1 x Elderflint Notebook at £8.95 (895 pence)\r\n"]
[20.6,"o","   4  add_to_cart    1 x Dunlin Merino Socks at £11.50 (1150 pence)\r\n"]
[20.9,"o","   5  get_quote      quote_000001, total £20.45 (2045 pence), expires 2026-10-25T09:15:00.000Z\r\n"]
[21.2,"o","   6  place_order    mandate accepted; order order_000001 is paid\r\n"]
[21.5,"o","\r\n"]
[21.8,"o","THE ORDER — paid, in one call\r\n"]
[22.1,"o","  order_000001 — paid\r\n"]
[22.4,"o","    1 x Elderflint Notebook             £8.95 (895 pence)\r\n"]
[22.7,"o","    1 x Dunlin Merino Socks             £11.50 (1150 pence)\r\n"]
[23,"o","    total                               £20.45 (2045 pence)\r\n"]
[23.3,"o","  Mandate budget: £20.45 (2045 pence) spent of £50.00 (5000 pence), £29.55 (2955 pence) left\r\n"]
[23.6,"o","  The ledger moves only after the rail captures (D45), so a refused\r\n"]
[23.9,"o","  order and a declined card both leave the budget untouched.\r\n"]
[24.2,"o","\r\n"]
[24.5,"o","THE PAYMENT RAIL — a stub; no real money, no network\r\n"]
[24.8,"o","  2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z rail=stub call=authorise outcome=ok order=order_000001 auth=auth_000001 amount=2045 GBP\r\n"]
[25.1,"o","  2026-01-01T00:00:01.000Z rail=stub call=capture outcome=ok order=order_000001 auth=auth_000001 amount=2045 GBP\r\n"]
[25.4,"o","  Timestamps are the stub’s synthetic epoch, not wall-clock time.\r\n"]
[25.7,"o","\r\n"]
[26,"o","THE AUDIT LOG — every mandate check and every settlement, pass or fail\r\n"]
[26.3,"o","  2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  allow             2045 GBP  agent-buyer-1 -> merchant-demo  mandate 11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111  -\r\n"]
[26.6,"o","  2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  paid              2045 GBP  order order_000001  mandate 11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111  -\r\n"]
[26.9,"o","  2 entries. Append-only: nothing here is ever edited.\r\n"]
[27.2,"o","  A check names the two parties; a settlement names the order it paid.\r\n"]
[27.5,"o","\r\n"]
[29.8,"o","--------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n"]
[30.1,"o"," RUN 2 — the same basket, a lower threshold, so a human must confirm\r\n"]
[30.4,"o","--------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n"]
[30.7,"o","\r\n"]
[31,"o","THE MANDATE — what the principal signed\r\n"]
[31.3,"o","  principal-demo lets agent-buyer-1 spend at merchant-demo:\r\n"]
[31.6,"o","    up to £50.00 (5000 pence) in total\r\n"]
[31.9,"o","    at most £25.00 (2500 pence) in any one order\r\n"]
[32.2,"o","    in GBP and no other currency\r\n"]
[32.5,"o","    between 2026-10-25T00:00:00Z and 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z\r\n"]
[32.8,"o","    without asking up to £20.00 (2000 pence); above that a human must confirm\r\n"]
[33.1,"o","  Signed Ed25519 over the canonical claims. The merchant holds the\r\n"]
[33.4,"o","  issuer's public key, read from ACR_MANDATE_PUBLIC_KEY, and no other\r\n"]
[33.7,"o","  key material: the private key never leaves the issuer, and nothing\r\n"]
[34,"o","  derived from it is printed here.\r\n"]
[34.3,"o","\r\n"]
[34.6,"o","WHAT THE AGENT DID — one line per step\r\n"]
[34.9,"o","   1  list_products  10 products in the catalogue\r\n"]
[35.2,"o","   2  create_cart    cart_000001, empty\r\n"]
[35.5,"o","   3  add_to_cart    1 x Elderflint Notebook at £8.95 (895 pence)\r\n"]
[35.8,"o","   4  add_to_cart    1 x Dunlin Merino Socks at £11.50 (1150 pence)\r\n"]
[36.1,"o","   5  get_quote      quote_000001, total £20.45 (2045 pence), expires 2026-10-25T09:15:00.000Z\r\n"]
[36.4,"o","   6  place_order    above the threshold: order order_000001 held for a human\r\n"]
[36.7,"o","\r\n"]
[37,"o","THE AGENT STOPS HERE\r\n"]
[37.3,"o","  order                 order_000001 — awaiting_confirmation\r\n"]
[37.6,"o","  confirmation token    confirm_000001\r\n"]
[37.9,"o","  £20.45 (2045 pence) is above the £20.00 (2000 pence) this mandate allows\r\n"]
[38.2,"o","  without asking, so the merchant is holding the order and has handed\r\n"]
[38.5,"o","  back a token. The agent does not use it and does not try again: an\r\n"]
[38.8,"o","  agent that confirms its own order has removed the control it exists\r\n"]
[39.1,"o","  to respect (D74). Nothing has been charged.\r\n"]
[39.4,"o","\r\n"]
[39.7,"o",">>> THE HUMAN’S STEP — this is the principal, not the agent\r\n"]
[40,"o","  principal-demo now calls confirm_order with the token, on a separate\r\n"]
[40.3,"o","  connection that has never held the mandate. In a product this is\r\n"]
[40.6,"o","  the push notification, the e-mail link or the banking app prompt;\r\n"]
[40.9,"o","  here it is the demo making the call the agent would not make.\r\n"]
[41.2,"o","\r\n"]
[41.5,"o","THE ORDER — paid, after the human confirmed\r\n"]
[41.8,"o","  order_000001 — paid\r\n"]
[42.1,"o","    1 x Elderflint Notebook             £8.95 (895 pence)\r\n"]
[42.4,"o","    1 x Dunlin Merino Socks             £11.50 (1150 pence)\r\n"]
[42.7,"o","    total                               £20.45 (2045 pence)\r\n"]
[43,"o","  Mandate budget: £20.45 (2045 pence) spent of £50.00 (5000 pence), £29.55 (2955 pence) left\r\n"]
[43.3,"o","  The ledger moves only after the rail captures (D45), so a refused\r\n"]
[43.6,"o","  order and a declined card both leave the budget untouched.\r\n"]
[43.9,"o","\r\n"]
[44.2,"o","THE PAYMENT RAIL — a stub; no real money, no network\r\n"]
[44.5,"o","  2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z rail=stub call=authorise outcome=ok order=order_000001 auth=auth_000001 amount=2045 GBP\r\n"]
[44.8,"o","  2026-01-01T00:00:01.000Z rail=stub call=capture outcome=ok order=order_000001 auth=auth_000001 amount=2045 GBP\r\n"]
[45.1,"o","  Timestamps are the stub’s synthetic epoch, not wall-clock time.\r\n"]
[45.4,"o","\r\n"]
[45.7,"o","THE AUDIT LOG — every mandate check and every settlement, pass or fail\r\n"]
[46,"o","  2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  confirm_required  2045 GBP  agent-buyer-1 -> merchant-demo  mandate 22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222  -\r\n"]
[46.3,"o","  2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  confirm_required  2045 GBP  agent-buyer-1 -> merchant-demo  mandate 22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222  -\r\n"]
[46.6,"o","  2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  paid              2045 GBP  order order_000001  mandate 22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222  -\r\n"]
[46.9,"o","  3 entries. Append-only: nothing here is ever edited.\r\n"]
[47.2,"o","  A check names the two parties; a settlement names the order it paid.\r\n"]
[47.5,"o","  2 mandate checks and 1 settlement above.\r\n"]
[47.8,"o","  The policy was asked when the order was held and asked again when\r\n"]
[48.1,"o","  the token came back, because the window, the caps and the budget\r\n"]
[48.4,"o","  can all have moved in between (D83). The settlement is the payment\r\n"]
[48.7,"o","  they authorised between them.\r\n"]
[49,"o","\r\n"]
[51.3,"o","--------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n"]
[51.6,"o"," RUN 3 — five attempts to spend past the mandate\r\n"]
[51.9,"o","--------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n"]
[52.2,"o","\r\n"]
[52.5,"o","THE MANDATE — what the principal signed\r\n"]
[52.8,"o","  principal-demo lets agent-buyer-1 spend at merchant-demo:\r\n"]
[53.1,"o","    up to £50.00 (5000 pence) in total\r\n"]
[53.4,"o","    at most £25.00 (2500 pence) in any one order\r\n"]
[53.7,"o","    in GBP and no other currency\r\n"]
[54,"o","    between 2026-10-25T00:00:00Z and 2026-10-26T00:00:00Z\r\n"]
[54.3,"o","    without asking up to £30.00 (3000 pence); above that a human must confirm\r\n"]
[54.6,"o","  Signed Ed25519 over the canonical claims. The merchant holds the\r\n"]
[54.9,"o","  issuer's public key, read from ACR_MANDATE_PUBLIC_KEY, and no other\r\n"]
[55.2,"o","  key material: the private key never leaves the issuer, and nothing\r\n"]
[55.5,"o","  derived from it is printed here.\r\n"]
[55.8,"o","  The same limits as run 1, under a mandate id of its own. In each\r\n"]
[56.1,"o","  attempt below the agent presents this mandate (in attempt 5, with a\r\n"]
[56.4,"o","  field added), and each is printed with what the merchant answered\r\n"]
[56.7,"o","  and what it left behind.\r\n"]
[57,"o","\r\n"]
[57.3,"o","ATTEMPT 1 OF 5 — over the per-order cap\r\n"]
[57.6,"o","  tries        Gallowbrook Cafetiere, £27.50 (2750 pence), in one order\r\n"]
[57.9,"o","  the limit    at most £25.00 (2500 pence) in any one order\r\n"]
[58.2,"o","  refused      mandate_refused [per_transaction_cap_exceeded]\r\n"]
[58.5,"o","  why          2750 is above this mandate's per-transaction cap of 2500 GBP\r\n"]
[58.8,"o","  1 audit line:\r\n"]
[59.1,"o","    2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  refuse            2750 GBP  agent-buyer-1 -> merchant-demo  mandate 33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333  per_transaction_cap_exceeded\r\n"]
[59.4,"o","  money        0 rail calls; spent £0.00 (0 pence), unchanged\r\n"]
[59.7,"o","\r\n"]
[60,"o","BETWEEN ATTEMPTS 1 AND 2 — two orders the mandate does cover\r\n"]
[60.3,"o","  order_000001 — paid, £20.45 (2045 pence), quote quote_000002\r\n"]
[60.6,"o","  order_000002 — paid, £20.45 (2045 pence), quote quote_000003\r\n"]
[60.9,"o","  Each one is Elderflint Notebook and Dunlin Merino Socks,\r\n"]
[61.2,"o","  the basket of runs 1 and 2.\r\n"]
[61.5,"o","  Mandate budget: £40.90 (4090 pence) spent of £50.00 (5000 pence), £9.10 (910 pence) left\r\n"]
[61.8,"o","  Run 3 means to pay nothing else. Each attempt below is measured on\r\n"]
[62.1,"o","  its own, from just before it to just after it.\r\n"]
[62.4,"o","\r\n"]
[62.7,"o","ATTEMPT 2 OF 5 — over the budget left\r\n"]
[63,"o","  tries        Elderflint Notebook and Dunlin Merino Socks,\r\n"]
[63.3,"o","               £20.45 (2045 pence), the basket of runs 1 and 2\r\n"]
[63.6,"o","  the limit    £9.10 (910 pence) left of the £50.00 (5000 pence) in total\r\n"]
[63.9,"o","  refused      mandate_refused [budget_exceeded]\r\n"]
[64.2,"o","  why          2045 is more than the 910 GBP left of this mandate's total cap of 5000\r\n"]
[64.5,"o","  1 audit line:\r\n"]
[64.8,"o","    2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  refuse            2045 GBP  agent-buyer-1 -> merchant-demo  mandate 33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333  budget_exceeded\r\n"]
[65.1,"o","  money        0 rail calls; spent £40.90 (4090 pence), unchanged\r\n"]
[65.4,"o","\r\n"]
[65.7,"o","ATTEMPT 3 OF 5 — at a merchant the mandate does not name\r\n"]
[66,"o","  tries        Elderflint Notebook and Dunlin Merino Socks,\r\n"]
[66.3,"o","               £20.45 (2045 pence), at merchant-other\r\n"]
[66.6,"o","  the limit    good at merchant-demo and nowhere else; merchant-other\r\n"]
[66.9,"o","               trusts the same issuer, so the signature holds\r\n"]
[67.2,"o","  refused      mandate_refused [merchant_mismatch]\r\n"]
[67.5,"o","  why          this mandate is good at merchant-demo, not at merchant-other\r\n"]
[67.8,"o","  1 audit line:\r\n"]
[68.1,"o","    2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  refuse            2045 GBP  agent-buyer-1 -> merchant-other  mandate 33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333  merchant_mismatch\r\n"]
[68.4,"o","  money        0 rail calls; spent £40.90 (4090 pence), unchanged\r\n"]
[68.7,"o","\r\n"]
[69,"o","ATTEMPT 4 OF 5 — a replay of an order already paid\r\n"]
[69.3,"o","  tries        place_order again with quote_000003, which order_000002 paid\r\n"]
[69.6,"o","  the limit    a quote is good for one order (D64, D127)\r\n"]
[69.9,"o","  refused      quote_already_ordered\r\n"]
[70.2,"o","  why          quote quote_000003 has already been ordered as order_000002 (paid)\r\n"]
[70.5,"o","  audit line   none: refused before the mandate check (D65, D127)\r\n"]
[70.8,"o","  money        0 rail calls; spent £40.90 (4090 pence), unchanged\r\n"]
[71.1,"o","\r\n"]
[71.4,"o","ATTEMPT 5 OF 5 — the mandate with a field added after signing\r\n"]
[71.7,"o","  tries        Elderflint Notebook, £8.95 (895 pence), within the\r\n"]
[72,"o","               £9.10 (910 pence) left, with \"extra_budget_minor\": 5000\r\n"]
[72.3,"o","               added to the mandate after it was signed\r\n"]
[72.6,"o","  the limit    every field but the signature is signed (D23)\r\n"]
[72.9,"o","  refused      mandate_refused [signature_invalid]\r\n"]
[73.2,"o","  why          the mandate was not signed by the expected issuer, or has been changed since\r\n"]
[73.5,"o","  1 audit line:\r\n"]
[73.8,"o","    2026-10-25T09:00:00.000Z  refuse            895 GBP  agent-buyer-1 -> merchant-demo  mandate 33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333  signature_invalid\r\n"]
[74.1,"o","  money        0 rail calls; spent £40.90 (4090 pence), unchanged\r\n"]
[74.4,"o","\r\n"]
[74.7,"o","THE INVARIANT — read off both ledgers and both rail logs\r\n"]
[75,"o","  5 attempts, 5 refused. Money moved by them: £0.00 (0 pence).\r\n"]
[75.3,"o","  Rail calls they caused: 0. Added to the ledger: £0.00 (0 pence).\r\n"]
[75.6,"o","  No attempt reached the rail, and the ledger moves only after the\r\n"]
[75.9,"o","  rail captures (D45), so none of them could move it.\r\n"]
